    "fatGrams": 17.5
  },
  "ingredients": [
    "1/4 cup almond flour",
    "1/4 cup coconut flour",
    "1 teaspoon ground cinnamon",
    "1/4 teaspoon salt",
    "1/2 teaspoon baking soda",
    "3 large egg",
    "1/4 cup erythritol",
    "1 tablespoon lemon juice",
    "1 tablespoon unsweetened carton coconut milk",
    "1/2 teaspoon vanilla extract",
    "1/2 teaspoon almond extract",
    "1/4 teaspoon liquid stevia",
    "1/2 teaspoon apple cider vinegar",
    "1/4 cup butter",
    "2 teaspoon red food coloring",
    "1/4 cup erythritol (powdered)",
    "4 ounce cream cheese (softened)",
    "4 tablespoon butter (softened)",
    "2 tablespoon heavy whipping cream",
    "1 teaspoon red food coloring"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 335F. Put a sifter on top of a large mixing bowl. Add almond flour,coconut flour, cinnamon, salt and baking soda.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/almond-lemon-sandwich-cakes/#wprm-recipe-50833-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2145536.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sift the ingredients until everything is fine and powdery.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/almond-lemon-sandwich-cakes/#wprm-recipe-50833-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2145537.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a mixing bowl, crack the eggs, then add erythritol, lemon juice, coconut milk, vanilla extract, almond extract, liquid stevia, and apple cider vinegar.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/almond-lemon-sandwich-cakes/#wprm-recipe-50833-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2145540.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Microwave the butter for the cakes for about 30 seconds.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/almond-lemon-sandwich-cakes/#wprm-recipe-50833-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2145538.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add butter to the wet ingredients and then add food coloring.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/almond-lemon-sandwich-cakes/#wprm-recipe-50833-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2145542.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir the ingredients well, making sure that the eggs are thoroughly broken.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/almond-lemon-sandwich-cakes/#wprm-recipe-50833-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2145543.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mix the wet ingredients into the dry ingredients using a hand mixer. Do this until you end up with a fluffy looking batter.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/almond-lemon-sandwich-cakes/#wprm-recipe-50833-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2145545.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Divide the batter between the holes in a non-stick muffin top pan. (You may also find this sold as a Whoopie Pie pan.) Spread the mixture in each muffin top mold.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/almond-lemon-sandwich-cakes/#wprm-recipe-50833-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2145546.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake for 17-18 minutes or until a toothpick comes out dry. You just want to have a slight browning around the edges.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/almond-lemon-sandwich-cakes/#wprm-recipe-50833-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2145549.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove from the muffin top pan and let cool on a cooling rack for 5 minutes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/almond-lemon-sandwich-cakes/#wprm-recipe-50833-step-0-9",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2145551.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slice the cakes in half using a bread knife. Bring some additional butter to a boil in a pan.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/almond-lemon-sandwich-cakes/#wprm-recipe-50833-step-0-10",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2145555.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add your muffin tops and fry on each side for about 1-2 minutes. You want to get these browned.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/almond-lemon-sandwich-cakes/#wprm-recipe-50833-step-0-11",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2145557.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Let the muffin tops cool while you make the icing.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/almond-lemon-sandwich-cakes/#wprm-recipe-50833-step-0-12",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2145558.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a mixing bowl, combine the butter (for the icing) and cream cheese.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/almond-lemon-sandwich-cakes/#wprm-recipe-50833-step-0-13",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2135437.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Powder the erythritol for the icing in a spice grinder. Let settle a few moments before removing the lid.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/almond-lemon-sandwich-cakes/#wprm-recipe-50833-step-0-14",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2135440.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cream the butter and cream cheese together until smooth.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/almond-lemon-sandwich-cakes/#wprm-recipe-50833-step-0-15",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2135438.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add heavy cream to the icing and continue mixing until smooth again.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/almond-lemon-sandwich-cakes/#wprm-recipe-50833-step-0-16",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2135439.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add powdered erythritol and red food coloring, then continue mixing. Continue adding food coloring until desired color is achieved.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/almond-lemon-sandwich-cakes/#wprm-recipe-50833-step-0-17",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2135442.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Spread icing between 2 pieces of almond lemon cake like a sandwich. Garnish with lemon zest and pistachios.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/almond-lemon-sandwich-cakes/#wprm-recipe-50833-step-0-18",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2145566.jpg"
    }
  ],
